## 🎓 GETTING STARTED WITH TASK 12

### Step 1: Review Baseline Data
```bash
# Review performance baseline
cat docs/PERFORMANCE_BASELINE.md

# Review optimization opportunities
cat docs/OPTIMIZATION_OPPORTUNITIES.md

# Check profiling data
python -c "from common.profiling import print_profiling_stats; print_profiling_stats()"
```

### Step 2: Design Activation Cache
```bash
# Create cache design document
vim docs/CACHE_DESIGN.md

# Key decisions:
# - Cache key generation strategy
# - Eviction policy (LRU recommended)
# - Memory limits (500MB recommended)
# - Thread safety approach
```

### Step 3: Implement ActivationCache
```bash
# Create cache implementation
vim common/activation_cache.py

# Key components:
# - Cache storage (dict + OrderedDict for LRU)
# - Cache operations (get, put, evict)
# - Statistics tracking
# - Thread safety (locks)
```

### Step 4: Integrate with Worker
```bash
# Modify worker inference
vim worker/inference_engine.py

# Integration points:
# - Check cache before forward pass
# - Store activations after forward pass
# - Cache invalidation on model changes
```

### Step 5: Add Tests
```bash
# Create comprehensive tests
vim tests/test_activation_cache.py

# Test coverage:
# - Cache hit/miss scenarios
# - Eviction policy correctness
# - Thread safety
# - Performance overhead
```

